================================================================================
=== REASONING ===
================================================================================

Why this design preserves ADR-015 (I1, I3, I4, I5, I6, I7, I10) plus the
methodology principles P9 (registry), P6 (guard + withAiFeature/useAiEnabled),
P10 (baseline coexistence), P11 (wired-or-absent), and P12 (no placeholder
buttons):

I1 — default-off
  The registry entry sets DefaultOn:false. New users land in
  ai_mode='off' with the toggle off; the component is absent and the
  backend route returns 404. No toggle state was changed by this commit.

I3 — baseline intact
  BatteryHealthPage's deterministic Capacity Trend & Prediction chart,
  hero metric cards, range trend chart, charge level distribution,
  insights panel, and recommendations panel are unchanged. The AI
  narrator is layered ABOVE the hero (rendered inside FadeIn at L428),
  not in place of any existing content. When the page is in off mode,
  the FadeIn still renders without the AI section because withAiFeature
  returns null inside the FadeIn child slot.

I4 — zero egress
  No new outbound network call exists in the ai_mode='off' code path.
  The fetch in the component only fires when the user clicks Narrate,
  which requires the gate (handled by withAiFeature) to have already
  returned non-null. In off mode the component never mounts, so the
  body, the useMemo, the useAiStream hook, and the click handler are
  all unreachable. The off-mode invariant test asserts the testid is
  absent — this is the canonical zero-egress proof for SPAs.

I5 — hidden UI
  withAiFeature returns null when useAiEnabled('battery-health-forecast-narrative')
  is false. The data-testid='ai-feature-battery-health-forecast-narrative-root'
  marker only exists on the wrapping div emitted by the HOC, so when
  the HOC returns null the marker is absent from the DOM. The off-mode
  test asserts queryByTestId returns null.

I6 — 404 routes
  The backend handler is wrapped in ai.GuardedHandler('battery-health-forecast-narrative')
  which short-circuits with 404 when the user's settings.ai_mode='off'
  OR the per-feature toggle is off. This was unchanged by this commit;
  the Go-side test ai_battery_health_handler_test.go covers it.

I7 — per-feature
  The HOC argument is a literal string 'battery-health-forecast-narrative'
  matching the registry entry's ID. Toggling the feature off (with
  ai_mode='cloud' or 'local') causes useAiEnabled to return false →
  HOC returns null → testid absent → backend returns 404 because
  ai.GuardedHandler also reads the per-feature toggle. The off-mode
  test exercises the per-feature toggle off case explicitly (case 3).

I10 — type system
  - Component body uses `{ vehicle_id: number }` matching the handler's
    parseBatteryHealthNarrateBody (which uses DisallowUnknownFields and
    requires vehicle_id > 0).
  - Vehicle ID is normalized to numeric via Number(vehicleId) and
    guarded with Number.isFinite + > 0 before enabling the button.
  - useAiStream is typed; AiOutputPanel takes (text, state, error)
    discriminated union from F5.
  - tsc --noEmit runs clean (see GATE).

I12 — client/bg (this slice does NOT add chunks/jobs/push/storage)
  The Off-mode contract section of the prompt declares:
      New background jobs:    none
      New push kinds:         none
      Service worker chunks:  ai-battery-health-forecast-narrative
      Client storage keys:    none
  The chunk is the route-level lazy-loaded chunk for the AI surface;
  it is automatically tree-shaken when withAiFeature returns null.
  No new ServiceWorker registration, no new IndexedDB schema, no new
  localStorage key was introduced by this commit.

P9 — registry coverage (unchanged from f6a607106)
  All RouteSet fields are explicit, including JobNames:[] and
  PushKinds:[]. aivet validates registry coverage and reports
  "OK — 22 AI route(s), 20 feature(s) in registry, TS mirror in sync".

P6 — guard + withAiFeature
  Backend: ai.GuardedHandler('battery-health-forecast-narrative')
  Frontend: withAiFeature('battery-health-forecast-narrative', InnerSection)

P10 — baseline coexistence
  Selection happens at composition time in BatteryHealthPage: the page
  always renders the deterministic chart + insights; the AI narrator
  HOC renders null in off mode, so it is purely additive. There is no
  branching inside the chart's data computation or in the
  battery-degradation handler.

P11 — wired-or-absent / P12 — no-placeholder-buttons
  This is the focus of this commit. The previous placeholder violated
  both: it shipped a literal-disabled button + "future slice" comment.
  The replacement:
    - Imports useAiStream from @/hooks/useAiStream
    - References the registered backend endpoint via url='/ai/battery/health/narrate'
    - Computed disabled prop: `disabled={!canGenerate}` where
      canGenerate = haveInputs && stream.state !== 'streaming'
    - Zero placeholder strings (verified by grep below)
    - The on-mode wiring test proves the click actually opens an SSE
      stream against the registered backend route

User-prefs middleware
  userPrefsMiddleware (in internal/api/ai_routes.go) already runs on
  the entire /api/v1/ai/* subtree. The dispatcher emits a second
  system message instructing the model to narrate in user display
  units. This slice does NOT duplicate that plumbing in the strategy
  or handler. The query_battery_health_forecast tool emits aggregate
  numeric battery metrics (state-of-health %, cycle count, projected
  capacity Wh) — capacity is already in SI Wh and capacity-percentage
  is unitless, so no temperature-style display-unit pre-computation
  is required. (cToFPtr-style precedent is preserved in
  drive_coaching.go for slices that DO emit Celsius.)

Forbidden patterns explicitly avoided
  - No legacy unit-suffixed Go field added (Phase-48 SI canonical) ✓
  - No /api hooks bypassed; the on-mode test verifies POST goes through
    the standard /api/v1/ai/... router ✓
  - No direct provider import from feature code; all calls go through
    the strategy + dispatcher ✓
  - No raw SQL in the tool; the tool calls the existing
    BatteryDegradationHandler service ✓
  - No new background job, push kind, ServiceWorker chunk, or storage
    key beyond the chunk declared in the registry ✓

